    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as the undisputed cornerstone of the lineup. His elite 80.13 score is anchored by a prime leadoff spot and a +14% dynamic platoon boost against Dobbins, making him our primary target for stolen base production\u2014a critical category as we press for the top of the standings. Alongside him, **Yordan Alvarez** (62.19) and **Kyle Schwarber** (61.18) provide high-floor stability; while **Yordan Alvarez** faces a tougher test against the efficient arm of Bryan Woo, his elite xwOBA of 0.465 allows us to overlook the unfavorable SP skill delta. **Junior Caminero** (60.55) also grades out strongly, benefiting from a favorable batting order position that offsets the park-factor headwinds in his matchup against Rogers.\n\nThe optimization process was most difficult at the MI/UTIL threshold, where **Dillon Dingler** (37.83) narrowly missed the cut. Despite the park factor favoring his matchup against Burke, the combination of a sharp -15% dynamic platoon penalty and our strict internal \"Zebras Floor\" of 40.0 forced him to the bench in favor of **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (51.76). We are monitoring the SP_xERA closely across the board; **Gary Sanchez** is the most significant risk in today\u2019s lineup, as he must navigate a daunting 2.77 xERA from Skubal. While his platoon advantage provides a slight cushion, his score of 41.99 sits dangerously close to the bench threshold, and we will be watching his early at-bats closely to ensure the Zebras don't leak points against an elite pitcher.",
